SECTION | KEY | VALUE
----------------------------------------
# rooms.pdl - the home's rooms and their doors. Every DOOR is a TELEPORT event (an on-touch page per door in each pet's event_pkg, `fire door_<room>_<dest>` -> pet_event.sh teleport <dest> <arrive_x>).
# ROOM | id | scene id | name            scene id = what ops/pet_scene.c draws (0 bedroom, 1 living room, 2 garden); new rooms need a drawing there, doors need only a DOOR row (the scene draws one door per row)
# DOOR | room | x (centre, px) | dest | arrive_x | auto     auto=1: a started pet may walk to this door on its own and teleport; auto=0: only you send it (the village needs the trainer)
ROOM | bedroom | 0 | Bedroom
ROOM | living  | 1 | Living room
ROOM | garden  | 2 | Garden (crops)
ROOM | roof    | 4 | Rooftop (looks over the village and the other pets houses)
DOOR | bedroom | 30  | village | 0   | auto=0
DOOR | bedroom | 334 | living  | 50  | auto=1
DOOR | living  | 30  | bedroom | 320 | auto=1
DOOR | living  | 338 | garden  | 50  | auto=1
DOOR | garden  | 30  | living  | 320 | auto=1
# two stairs-up doors lead to the rooftop (one in the bedroom, one in the living room); the roof has a stairs-down door on each side
DOOR | bedroom | 182 | roof    | 60  | auto=1
DOOR | living  | 196 | roof    | 300 | auto=1
DOOR | roof    | 30  | bedroom | 182 | auto=1
DOOR | roof    | 334 | living  | 196 | auto=1
# PLATFORM | room | x0 | x1 | top y | name : furniture the pet may jump on and walk along (it never breaks anything); a started pet picks one now and then
PLATFORM | bedroom | 62  | 158 | 216 | bed
PLATFORM | bedroom | 206 | 302 | 216 | desk
PLATFORM | living  | 134 | 246 | 210 | sofa
PLATFORM | living  | 252 | 312 | 220 | tv stand
PLATFORM | roof | 168 | 214 | 214 | chimney
